{
  "about": "What a stream is made of (StreamSpecs) and how the apps say it, written by hand: the same file for Android's StreamSpecsTest and Apple's StreamSpecsTests. `resolution`: a picture's size and its class (null: unknown). `audio`: a sound's codec, channels and Atmos, as the facts line and a chip say it. `codecs`: the names ffprobe, a FourCC or a MIME subtype give a codec, and the conventional name. `badges`: a version's name and specs, its facts line's badges and what a screen reader says (English). `audio` rows may give the provider's `layout` (channel_layout), said before the count. `layoutNames`: a provider's channel_layout and how the apps say it. `merge`: what the player measured over the provider's, field by field (Atmos only ever added, a layout kept only where it agrees with the channels). `measured`: readings of one stream in turn, whether each is kept and what is kept at the end (the first stays unless the picture grew). `audioPick`: the sound the player measures among a stream's tracks (the default, else the most channels). `provider`: the `info` object of a panel's get_vod_info and the specs read from it (null: nothing). A field of `specs` left out is unknown. Invented values only.",
